      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Tôi có đặt chỗ is the phrase to keep ready for \"I have a booking\" in times, dates, tickets, waits, and bookings. This is for when the booking exists and you need staff to find it first. Start with the booking before you ask about timing changes. It works best when you focus on naming the concrete item or problem first so staff can choose the next action. After you say it, listen for a request to see the item, a direction to another desk, or a practical next step; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
